<title>USA: XOMA to receive $8.5 mln from Genentech.</title>
<headline>XOMA to receive $8.5 mln from Genentech.</headline>
<dateline>BERKELEY, Calif. 1996-12-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>XOMA Corp said it will receive an $8.5 million payment from Genentech Inc to cover 1997 development expenses on the hu1124 monoclonal antibody product. XOMA currently is testing the product in Phase 1 safety trials in patients with moderate to severe psoriasis.</p>
<p>HU1124 is being jointly developed by XOMA and Genentech as a treatment for psoriasis and organ transplant rejection.</p>
</text>
